From d3520c51f88c3d7173990d72d9ad89be179c7542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:05:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pf: also deliver IPv6 replies of redirected connections to
 the host's own address

The IPv4 change before this one exempted replies of a host's connection to
one of its own addresses, redirected by an outbound rule to another host,
from ip_input()'s source address validation. ip6_input() has the same
check (net.inet6.ip6.source_address_validation) and dropped the IPv6
replies the same way: a Kubernetes node reaching its own NodePort on an
IPv6 address timed out on a dual-stack cluster. Mark them M_FASTFWD_OURS
too.

Tested on 15.1 arm64: curl from a node to its own IPv6 address and a
NodePort redirected to a pod on the other node: succeeds (before: timed
out; with the sysctl off it succeeded, confirming the cause).
---
 sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
index a9182b491..a154c7061 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
+++ b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
@@ -11254,6 +11254,14 @@ pf_test(sa_family_t af, int dir, int pflags, struct ifnet *ifp, struct mbuf **m0
 	    in_localip(pd.src->v4) && in_localip(pd.dst->v4))
 		pd.m->m_flags |= M_FASTFWD_OURS;
 #endif
+#ifdef INET6
+	/* The same for IPv6 (ip6_input()'s net.inet6.ip6.source_address_validation). */
+	if (dir == PF_IN && action == PF_PASS && af == AF_INET6 && s != NULL &&
+	    s->direction == PF_OUT &&
+	    s->key[PF_SK_WIRE] != s->key[PF_SK_STACK] &&
+	    in6_localip(&pd.src->v6) && in6_localip(&pd.dst->v6))
+		pd.m->m_flags |= M_FASTFWD_OURS;
+#endif
 
 	if (action == PF_PASS && r->divert.port && !PACKET_LOOPED(&pd)) {
 		mtag = m_tag_alloc(MTAG_PF_DIVERT, 0,
